{"seq":19,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-conservative-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T07:57:10.751Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"bd05ebcc2bffd39827d4e2ba61a2d4d9dcabf0e49a3bedab28e7d5951f77b7ba","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Here's what I found. One caveat first: neither source names Marrow Fieldworks next to a ticket number. The tickets below are tied to a \"dealer account\", and I'm reading that as Fieldworks from the context. Please check that before the call.\n\n**From Moss's notes** (the \"Central handoffs next week\" digest, 2 Jan 2026, which says Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on 5 Jan 2026):\n- **#4409**: the Gatehouse Check-In report keeps timing out at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). Listed as an open ticket on \"Pree's dealer account\" before the handoff.\n- **#4412**: a small glitch in the driver SMS prompt when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots. Same account.\n\n**From #central-random** (13 Oct, your own message at 09:27):\n- **#8841**: West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. Hollis had called it \"Tobias's dealer account.\"\n\n**Left out on purpose:** FR-882 (the pallet-jack icon request, in the same digest) and PD-4821 (in #central-team) both belong to **Marrow Agrisupply**. That's a different account, so I didn't count them.\n\nThat's everything in Moss's Central and North digests and in #central-random. There's no account folder for Marrow Fieldworks in the shared files, so I couldn't check these against a ticket list."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
